      "side": 1,
      "message": "This works, but I\u0027m not sure we want to do something like this yet, so I made it WIP for now. \n\nSome thoughts: doing it at this level in Gerrit does enable it for everything, but doing at other levels can offload more stuff asynchronously. For example, in jgit, CancellableDigestOutputStream also does some checksum calculations, which can also benefit from being offloaded. Another factor is that the TimeoutOutputStream constantly resets itself before and after every write, and since this class actually does some additional buffering, it can reduce that workload if it were above the TimeoutOutputStream (here in BaseCommand, it is below that). However, we have already mitigated most of the impact of TimeoutOutputStream, so it probably would not help that situation anymore. \n\nYou could say that this approach really needs a good problematic use case to tackle. For now, I am not convinced that this is worth it, but I thought that it would be valuable to test in more places since it might be more beneficial in other use cases which I have not tried yet.",
      "revId": "d322afc18989084f4d61f829c6c1a7488074e6a4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
